abstract: >-
  Six lessons implementing machine learning fundamentals in numpy — least
  squares by three solvers, gradient descent, regularisation, logistic
  regression, trees and ensembles, and evaluation. Every estimator is pinned
  by a test at one of three tiers: exact agreement with an independent
  reference, properties that hold exactly without any reference, or recovery
  of parameters known before the data existed. Every number quoted in the
  lessons is injected from the code by a report command, and continuous
  integration regenerates them on a different machine and fails the build on
  any drift, so the prose cannot disagree with what the code does.
